{"reference":"1 Samuel 4","book":"1 Samuel","chapter":4,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Ark in the Larger Narrative","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Israel brings the ark into the camp expecting it to guarantee victory, but the larger ark narrative rejects that expectation. The LORD’s power is not dependent on an Israelite army or on Israel’s possession of the ark: the story goes on to portray the LORD judging Philistine gods and communities even after the ark has been captured.","verse_refs":["1 Samuel 1","1 Samuel 10:1-27","1 Samuel 11:1-15","1 Samuel 12:1-25","1 Samuel 13:1-23","1 Samuel 14:1-52","1 Samuel 15:1-35","1 Samuel 16:1-23","1 Samuel 17:1-58","1 Samuel 18:1-30","1 Samuel 19:1-24","1 Samuel 20:1-42","1 Samuel 21:1-15","1 Samuel 22:1-23","1 Samuel 23:1-29","1 Samuel 24:1-22","1 Samuel 25:1-44","1 Samuel 26:1-25","1 Samuel 27:1-12","1 Samuel 28:1-25","1 Samuel 29:1-11","1 Samuel 2:1-36","1 Samuel 30:1-31","1 Samuel 31:1-13","1 Samuel 3:1-21","1 Samuel 5:1-12","1 Samuel 6:1-21","1 Samuel 7:1-17","1 Samuel 8:1-22","1 Samuel 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_1_samuel_004_b3f97ffbd2f26cf7336575c6"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"inference"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}